[{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.774890942,"data":"# Kaggle kernel agent guide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775058141,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775067803,"data":"This file travels inside every kernel that `scripts/kaggle_run.py` pushes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775072359,"data":"and is printed at the top of its log. The repository's root AGENTS.md owns\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775076266,"data":"every rule; this guide states what a Kaggle kernel is for, what it runs on,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775080256,"data":"and what it must prove before its output counts.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.77508338,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775086538,"data":"## What runs where\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775089675,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775092992,"data":"| Substrate | Runs | Never runs |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775096175,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775099561,"data":"| Kaggle GPU kernel (Aer on GPU) | every simulation of 14 qubits or fewer: noise simulations under a retained calibration export, design power analyses, parameter sweeps | IBM jobs; anything needing an IBM credential |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775104729,"data":"| Kaggle CPU in the same kernel | transpilation, package builds, the hypercomplex table extraction | |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775108571,"data":"| Kaggle TPU (v5e-8 shape) | JAX code only; Aer has no TPU backend, so no repository simulation uses it | Qiskit or Aer |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775112554,"data":"| Kaggle Gemma models (attached through `model_sources`) | text tasks on request | evidence: a language-model answer supports no physical or mathematical claim |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775116613,"data":"| IBM Heron (ibm_fez, ibm_kingston, ibm_marrakesh) | 15 or more qubits, or a question about a named device qubit, only after the owner approves a written case | simulations |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775120785,"data":"| GitHub Actions CPU | the CPU replay gate that re-derives a reduced case of each Kaggle result | GPU work |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775124991,"data":"| Build host (Arch, RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB) | development, dry runs, calibration exports, the Arch-packaged hypercomplex stack and SageMath | runs the routing rule sends to Kaggle |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775129188,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775132685,"data":"## Every kernel's phases\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775136273,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775139333,"data":"`kaggle_kernel/kernel_main.py` writes one JSON file per phase into\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775142996,"data":"`/kaggle/working/output`:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.77514618,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775149813,"data":"1. `environment.json`: Python and package versions, CPU model and cores,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775153844,"data":"   RAM, working disk, every GPU (name, memory, driver, compute capability),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775157663,"data":"   CUDA driver version, TPU devices, Aer devices and attached models.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775161415,"data":"2. `hypercomplex.json`: the hypercomplex stack. The kernel fetches the eight\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775165277,"data":"   pinned archives (sha256-checked), installs them through the PKGBUILD\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775169046,"data":"   recipes in `scripts/algebra_package_tables.py`, runs `--extract`, and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775183454,"data":"   stops with exit code 3 unless the regenerated\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775187296,"data":"   `docs/evidence/algebra_packages/tables.json` equals the retained bytes.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775191055,"data":"   The build host passes the same test against its Arch packages, so a run\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775195053,"data":"   that reaches its entry used the same algebra code as the host.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775198826,"data":"3. `capacity.json` (smoke kernels): the widest GHZ circuit each Aer method\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775202564,"data":"   runs on the GPU.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775206204,"data":"4. The entry's stdout, stderr, exit code and changed files.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775209935,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775213448,"data":"## Package stack\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775217024,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775220556,"data":"| Package | Pin | Kernel source |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775224488,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.77522819,"data":"| qiskit | 2.5.2 | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775231842,"data":"| qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 | 0.17.2 (the CUDA 12 `qiskit-aer-gpu` stops at 0.15.1 and has no Python 3.13 wheel) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775235861,"data":"| hypercomplex, hypercomplex-engine, hypercomplex-algebra, Cayley-Calculator, octonion, mathdunders | 0.3.4, 0.5.0, 0.2.0.2, 1.3.1, 0.1.0, 0.4.2 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775240005,"data":"| cayley-dickson, SplitOct | commits abf96e7, e29e72f | GitHub archive, sha256-pinned, PKGBUILD recipe |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.77524385,"data":"| numpy-quaternion | 2024.0.13 | PyPI (Cayley-Calculator runtime) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775247308,"data":"| numpy, scipy, sympy, pandas, torch | Kaggle image versions, recorded per run | Kaggle image |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775250542,"data":"| SageMath | 10.10 | build host only; a computation that needs Sage stays there |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775254079,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775257284,"data":"## Rules\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775260604,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775264006,"data":"- A kernel is private, has GPU and internet enabled, and holds no IBM\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775267228,"data":"  credential. Noise comes from a retained\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775270565,"data":"  `gororoba_quantum/calibration_snapshot.py` export.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775276256,"data":"- The entry reads `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE` and selects the GPU through it.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775280365,"data":"- An output is a numerical simulation. It enters\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775284144,"data":"  `docs/state/research_state.json` only after a CPU replay gate re-derives\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775287597,"data":"  a reduced case.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775290997,"data":"- Measured limits of each machine shape are in\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775294401,"data":"  `docs/notes/kaggle/substrates.md`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":41.775297853,"data":"\n"}
